  "answer": {
    "summary": "Tesla reports revenue under two XBRL concepts because the SEC updated its taxonomy to reflect ASC 606, adding a new concept for revenue from contracts with customers excluding assessed taxes. The legacy 'Revenues' concept continues to capture total GAAP revenue for all years, while the newer concept should be used for contract‑revenue‑excluding‑taxes starting from the year Tesla adopted ASC 606 (FY 2018) when that concept becomes populated.",
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Tesla's revenue facts table contains two distinct XBRL concepts: 'Revenues' and 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax'.",
        "evidence": ["E-50d25e"]
      },
      {
        "text": "For fiscal years 2011 through the latest year in the data, the 'Revenues' concept appears with non‑zero counts (e.g., 2011 FY 14, 2011 Q2 4, 2012 FY 11, 2012 Q1 2, 2012 Q2 4) while the 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax' concept shows zero counts in the sampled periods.",
        "evidence": ["E-01109d"]
      }
    ],
    "inferences": [
      {
        "text": "The presence of two concepts reflects the SEC's taxonomy update to incorporate ASC 606, requiring a separate element for revenue from contracts with customers excluding assessed taxes.",
        "basis": ["H-8edb42", "H-df72bc"]
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore, the 'Revenues' concept should be used for total GAAP revenue for all years, and the 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax' concept should be used for contract‑revenue‑excluding‑taxes starting from FY 2018 when Tesla adopted ASC 606 and that concept becomes populated.",
        "basis": ["H-8edb42", "H-df72bc", "claims"]
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis_verdicts": [
      {
        "id": "H-8edb42",
        "status": "supported",
        "evidence": ["E-01109d", "E-50d25e"],
        "why": "Shows two distinct concepts and indicates a temporal shift in usage consistent with a taxonomy update."
      },
      {
        "id": "H-8348d9",
        "status": "refuted",
        "evidence": ["E-01109d"],
        "why": "No fiscal period shows both concepts with non‑zero counts, which would be expected if duplicate filings caused the duplication."
      },
      {
        "id": "H-df72bc",
        "status": "supported",
        "evidence": ["E-01109d", "E-50d25e"],
        "why": "Matches the expectation that ASC 606 adoption (FY 2018) introduced a new concept while the legacy concept remained for total revenue."
      },
      {
        "id": "H-43efd2",
        "status": "open",
        "evidence": [],
        "why": "The data do not provide a breakdown of revenue streams (e.g., vehicle sales vs. credits) needed to evaluate this hypothesis."
      }
    ]
  },
  "carryover": {
    "COMPLETED": "Answered why Tesla uses two XBRL revenue concepts and which to use for which years.",
    "REMAINING": "",
    "DECISIONS": "Use 'Revenues' for total GAAP revenue all years; use 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax' for contract revenue excluding taxes where it appears (likely post‑2018).",
    "CONTEXT": "Answer based solely on evidence from edgar.revenue_facts and edgar.company_profiles tables."
  }
